 maybe the mission and values um  and then the rest of it you don't need  to worry about right away although  you're welcome to look  um but uh the contributor guy in the  code of contact should basically be  enough to get you uh ready to go and  start working contributing  uh and then how to help uh so again go  to github uh our network  x repository on github and we're looking  at you know lots of things but you know  algorithms and documentation so uh  you know the traveling salesman problem  was recently in the news  uh and we don't have the classic  christopher's algorithm  uh we also have some social network  analysis community detection but we  could use a lot more  uh many of us in the developer community  are interested in biological networks  and we'd love to see better support  um there's also been a lot of work  recently on gras there's  been a lot of discussion of work on  graph isomorphism so i think that this  will probably uh  we'll probably have some new graph  isomorphism algorithms implemented in  the next few months  um documentation so if you don't really  want to contribute to the code but uh  you're interested in doing some more  long-form documentation with  code we would love to have improved  gallery examples so you know  if you have your own uh you know data  set with your own  analysis and examples you might be able  to find a little  nice graphic and share it with others  we'd love to have that  we also are recently adding more of a  notebook binder style tutorial on how-to  documents which we'd love to see things  um you know for example domain-specific  introductions you know network x for  geospatial scientists or network ex for  neuroscientists or neuroimaging people  um as well as education materials so  thank you very much for listening and uh  we are going to have a sprint at this pi  day pi data global i hope to  you join us there and i hope to see you  guys on github as well  thanks a lot
 

